research/audit/wave11-judge-adjudications.jsonl-1-{"id":"cor-taylor-remainder-bound","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"003e540256ae9fbca1580dab85f55df303c19bc5659a8e9e95f8c67a0f3f484f","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"3727505d8318a08e271f9339f63a3aaceb6853ee2b57e272b67a48bc658d55e4","verdict_item_sha256":"d50d861e5f8c31de0bba0df933f66fa58ae792fa1964f9198efc5b64bda09bd1","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T15:55:40Z","note":"Terra correctly observes that Fact L1 names the linked Lagrange formula rather than restating it. This is a nonfatal citation-voice compression, not an unsupported inference: the cited corollary says verbatim, 'Under the hypotheses of thm-taylor-schlomilch-roche-remainder, there are points xi_L, xi_C between a and x such that', followed by the exact Lagrange formula used in step 1.1; the exact proof contract quotes that Statement and maps it to step 1.1. A reader closes the pointer immediately, so R1 forbids an edit."}
research/audit/wave11-judge-adjudications.jsonl-2-{"id":"thm-linearity-of-the-integral","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"3ce712cb0059ce09419262875e303bd305d313951b93ff7989f41b7dc0a93a33","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"5ddedcbca79ba5bf988a1a3b132e584d4a611897d1903879f7faed8341c96809","verdict_item_sha256":"a84c2e87990285e68fe31938594622b841932d5c4ada8dd4a1839bfe7e633334","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T15:55:40Z","note":"Terra identifies a genuine but nonfatal input-map compression: Fact L5 names only additivity and scaling although step 2.2 also uses finite-sum monotonicity. The same linked source states verbatim, 'If a_k <= b_k for all k < n then sum_{k<n} a_k <= sum_{k<n} b_k,' and the exact contract quotes that full Statement and maps the source to step 2.2. Multiplying each inequality by positive Delta_i and applying this clause closes the step in seconds. The proof is valid and R1 forbids an edit."}
research/audit/wave11-judge-adjudications.jsonl-3-{"id":"thm-linearity-of-the-integral","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"3ce712cb0059ce09419262875e303bd305d313951b93ff7989f41b7dc0a93a33","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"5ddedcbca79ba5bf988a1a3b132e584d4a611897d1903879f7faed8341c96809","verdict_item_sha256":"a84c2e87990285e68fe31938594622b841932d5c4ada8dd4a1839bfe7e633334","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T15:55:40Z","note":"DeepSeek's Archimedean objection is mathematically mistaken. The cited ordered-field definition states verbatim, 'For each $x \\in F$, exactly one of the following holds: $x \\in P$, or $x = 0$, or $-x \\in P$.' Fact L9 assumes |x| < eta for every positive real eta. If x were nonzero, trichotomy and the definition of absolute value make |x| itself positive, so substituting eta := |x| gives the contradiction |x| < |x|. No Archimedean theorem or least-upper-bound argument is used. Step 5.1 is exact and no edit is permitted."}
