research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log-1434084-+{"id":"ex-two-root-x-and-its-unbounded-derivative","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www2.hawaii.edu/~gradysw/apex/sec_derivative.html","https://faculty.gvsu.edu/boelkinm/Home/ACS/sec-6-5-improper.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that sqrt(x) is continuous, has derivative 1/(2sqrt(x)) for x>0, is not differentiable at zero, and has an unbounded derivative near zero. The item scales by 2 and packages those facts to explain why the proper Riemann FTC does not apply on [0,1].","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
