research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-40-{"id":"thm-ftc-first-part","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.cmu.edu/~gautam/c/2026-269/notes/rint.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that the integral function of a Riemann-integrable f is differentiable at every point where f is continuous, with derivative f at that point. The repository adds explicit one-sided endpoint language already fixed by its derivative definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-41-{"id":"thm-ftc-second-part","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.cmu.edu/~gautam/c/2026-269/notes/rint.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The sources state the Newton-Leibniz formula for a differentiable function whose derivative is Riemann integrable, with the same conclusion. The item's proof through the first FTC and constant-difference theorem is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-42-{"id":"cor-primitives-of-a-continuous-function","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Integral_calculus","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The sources give existence of the integral-function primitive, uniqueness up to an additive constant, and evaluation of definite integrals by any primitive. The item collects these standard consequences in one corollary and applies its endpoint convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-43-{"id":"thm-integration-by-parts","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.cmu.edu/~gautam/c/2026-269/notes/rint.html"],"rationale":"CMU Theorem 20 states the exact Riemann integration-by-parts theorem used here: differentiable u and v on [a,b], integrable derivatives, and the same boundary-term identity. The repository proof additionally makes integrability of the two products explicit.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-10"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-44-{"id":"thm-substitution","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.cmu.edu/~gautam/c/2026-269/notes/rint.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html"],"rationale":"The sources give change of variables for continuous f and a C^1 substitution. The item weakens C^1 to differentiability with Riemann-integrable derivative and uses the same oriented identity. Its proof through a primitive and the chain rule is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-45-{"id":"thm-second-mean-value-theorem-for-integrals","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Lebesgue_integral"],"rationale":"The source states Bonnet's second mean value formula for monotone g and integrable f, with the same endpoint coefficients and an intermediate xi, in the stronger Lebesgue setting. The item specializes it to bounded Riemann-integrable f and its oriented convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-46-{"id":"thm-nonnegative-continuous-with-zero-integral-vanishes","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/~rbm/18.100-F02.HMW/HMW7s.pdf","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_rintprop.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that a nonnegative continuous function on a compact interval with zero integral is identically zero. The item's positive-neighbourhood lower-bound proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-47-{"id":"thm-integral-test-for-series","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_impropriemann.html"],"rationale":"The source states the integral test for a positive decreasing function and its sampled series. The item reformulates convergence of the improper integral as boundedness of the proper-integral sequence indexed from zero, allows nonincreasing nonnegative f, and records explicit comparison inequalities.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:48:{"id":"rem-integral-conventions-and-scope","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"none","urls":[],"rationale":"This is a repository-specific convention and scope record, including reading-order statements and deliberate omissions. Alpha checked every linked target on current disk and repaired the stale scaffold-era Taylor-integral-remainder assignment: the current Taylor page explicitly excludes that form, so the ledger now records it as absent with no published destination.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-10"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-49-{"id":"ex-polynomial-integrals-by-the-ftc","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~demmel/ma128a_Spr02/LectureNotes/Integration.html"],"rationale":"The university notes state exactly integral_0^1 x^m dx=1/(m+1) for nonnegative integer m. The item translates the integer into the library's canonical real embedding and supplies local FTC and consistency checks.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-50-{"id":"ex-additivity-on-a-step-function","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"The particular two-level step function and its paired verification routes are a local worked construction. Splitting at 1 gives two constant integrals 1 and 3, and the displayed three-point Darboux partition gives matching sums after the single jump is isolated; the value 4 is directly verified.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-51-{"id":"ex-integral-test-applied-to-the-p-series","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_series.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_impropriemann.html"],"rationale":"The sources give the p-series threshold p>1 and the integral test. The item specializes to rational powers available in the library, indexes f_p(t)=(t+1)^{-p} from zero, and expresses improper convergence as boundedness of its proper-integral sequence. The mathematical threshold is sourced, but its last p=1 sentence falsely denies existence of a primitive and is proposed for repair.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-52-{"id":"ex-two-root-x-and-its-unbounded-derivative","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://clp.math.uky.edu/clp1/sec_def_deriv.html","https://faculty.gvsu.edu/boelkinm/Home/ACS/sec-6-5-improper.html"],"rationale":"The CLP university text computes (sqrt x)'=1/(2sqrt x) for x>0 and states that the derivative is undefined at zero; Active Calculus treats 1/sqrt x as an unbounded integrand at zero. The item scales by 2, proves the precise unbounded sequence, and packages those facts to explain why the proper Riemann FTC does not apply on [0,1].","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-10"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-53-{"id":"cex-an-integrable-function-with-no-primitive","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_ftc.html","https://math.colgate.edu/math323/dlantz/extras/notesC5.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the sign function's integral function as an absolute-value function and Darboux's theorem that derivatives cannot jump. The item packages these standard facts as an explicit refutation of the claim that every Riemann-integrable function has a primitive.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-54-{"id":"cex-a-function-with-a-primitive-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.sc.edu/girardi/m555/10S/diff-counterexs.pdf"],"rationale":"Olmsted's university-hosted differentiation counterexamples give the classical function x^2 sin(1/x^2), differentiable on a closed interval with an explicitly unbounded derivative. The published item names that classical witness and replaces its trigonometric oscillations by disjoint quartic bumps because trigonometric functions occur later in the library. The exact polynomial realization and its seam proof are local, but the mathematical counterexample is a recoverable source-backed alteration rather than an invented proposition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-10"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-55-{"id":"cex-a-composition-of-integrable-functions-that-is-not-integrable","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00591-022-00318-x"],"rationale":"The peer-reviewed source gives the same counterexample: Thomae's Riemann-integrable function composed with the integrable indicator of the positive range becomes Dirichlet's nonintegrable function. The repository's discontinuity-set verification is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-56-{"id":"cex-absolute-value-integrable-without-the-function","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"The signed Dirichlet function, equal to 1 on rationals and -1 on irrationals, is a standard counterexample: its absolute value is constant while every Darboux lower and upper sum differs. Search located the exact witness only in non-qualifying discussion sources; reputable texts located during the pass state Dirichlet nonintegrability but not this full signed claim. It therefore requires Alpha's independent established-knowledge concurrence and is not mislabeled as invented.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-09"}
